+# Q3 2026 Operating Brief
+
+## Executive summary
+
+Q3 was a solid quarter financially, with revenue of $720,000 against spend of
+$464,000, producing an operating surplus of $256,000. Support held a strong
+close rate of 93.7% across 1,250 opened tickets. The delivery team's project
+plan, run against the business-day rules and the single company holiday in
+the period, points to a launch date of 2026-10-23. Security resolved 76 of
+80 detected incidents, a 95.0% resolution rate. Overall the quarter shows
+healthy margins and stable operational execution, though see the Notes
+section for source-data discrepancies that should be corrected before these
+figures are circulated further.
+
+## Key figures
+
+| Metric | Value |
+|---|---:|
+| Q3 revenue | $720,000 |
+| Q3 spend | $464,000 |
+| Operating surplus | $256,000 |
+| Support close rate | 93.7% |
+| Launch date | 2026-10-23 |
+| Security resolution rate | 95.0% |
+
+## Notes
+
+Three of the four source packets contain a summary figure that does not
+match the underlying data, and the figures above use the recomputed
+(correct) values rather than the packets' stated summaries. These should be
+escalated to the respective teams so their dashboards and reports can be
+fixed:
+
+- **Finance:** the packet states total Q3 spend as $463,250, but the listed
+  spend categories (Payroll $286,400 + Infrastructure $81,750 + Contractors
+  $64,200 + Facilities $31,650) sum to $464,000 — a $750 discrepancy.
+- **Support:** the packet labels the Q3 close rate as 96.4%, but 1,171
+  closed tickets out of 1,250 opened computes to 93.7% — a 2.7-point gap.
+- **Delivery:** the packet states the launch date as 2026-10-22. Applying
+  the phase durations (Discovery 3, Build 6, QA 4, Release 1 business days,
+  each phase starting the next business day after the prior one ends) from
+  the 2026-10-05 start, and excluding the 2026-10-12 company holiday, the
+  plan actually lands on 2026-10-23.
+- **Security:** no discrepancy found; the stated 95.0% resolution rate
+  matches the underlying incident counts (76 of 80).
+
+Recommend leadership treat the finance and support figures above as
+provisional pending confirmation with those teams, and flag the delivery
+timeline slip of one business day to the project stakeholders.
